 "mandate_proposal.notes[0]": "Die Nutzung ist nicht erfasst. Gerechnet wird mit der strengsten der drei Varianten (Ein Zweit- oder Ferienobjekt, 30%), weil ein zu tiefes Ziel einem Haushalt sagt, es reiche, wenn es nicht reicht.",
 "mandate_proposal.notes[1]": "the household's stated yearly saving is 52,000; this goal's share is not stated, so the most it can receive (100.0%, 52,000 a year) is used: the required return and the curve's level are lower bounds until the share is stated",
 "mandate_proposal.notes[2]": "the goal's amount 1,800,000 is in today's francs (the request does not say; decision 7: today by default) and is inflated to its date at 1.00% a year (CHF, price level 1.0432): 1,877,752.48 in francs of the target date",
 "mandate_proposal.notes[3]": "the contribution is fixed in francs (the request does not say; decision 9: fixed by default), so its purchasing power falls by 1.00% a year",
 "mandate_proposal.notes[4]": "the risk profile also interpolates asset-class bounds {'Cash': {'lower': 0.0, 'upper': 0.2908934305670598}, 'Equity': {'lower': 0.0, 'upper': 0.4779578729895777}}; asset class is a policy dimension, so they are a suggestion for the curator and not a derived bound",
 "mandate_proposal.plausibility.ceiling_nominal": 0.04830265443948045,
 "mandate_proposal.plausibility.ceiling_real": 0.037923420237109165,
 "mandate_proposal.plausibility.ceiling_source": "approved by the owner (Nicolas, 29.09.2026, LBS-37), the table unchanged from its proposal in 1.4.0 (LBS-34): the most a portfolio at the risk profile's level can reasonably be planned to earn over the long run, real, a year; 2 % at the cautious end (about the long-run real return of Swiss government bonds), 5 % at the aggressive end (about the long-run real return of Swiss equities), linear in between; a plan that needs more than the long-run return of the asset class it may hold rests on luck",
